v class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-content-wrapper_3MziH"><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-background-wrapper_2UMSb"><div class="_Y3Itd_page-indicator-container_1X84N"><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-page-indicator_10KaA" data-hook="PageIndicator"></div></div><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-topbar_knKqX"><button data-popover-id="R14LV48YQR4Y65" class="_Y3Itd_close-button_2RG2d" data-hook="ReviewMediaPopoverCloseButton" data-mix-operations="ReviewMediaPopoverCloseButtonClickHandler" data-csa-c-type="element" data-csa-c-id="jolj3y-yn4tci-i4lpmv-v2o0y"><i class="a-icon a-icon-close-white a-icon-medium" role="presentation"></i></button></div><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-media-list-view-container_1kFg1" data-hook="ReviewMediaList"><button data-popover-id="R14LV48YQR4Y65" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-media-list-overlay_2x3M5" data-mix-operations="ReviewMediaPopoverNextMediaClickHandler"></button></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></span></li><li><span class="a-list-item"><div data-hook="reviewContainer" data-translatable="false" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-asin="B0B8SQKDCL" data-mobile="false" data-locale="en-US" data-localelanguagename="English" data-sourcelanguage="en-US" data-sourcelanguagename="English" data-iscustomerrecognized="true" data-iskindleapp="false" data-isandroidapp="false" data-isiosapp="false" data-ismshop="false" data-marketplaceid="ATVPDKIKX0DER"><div id="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-csa-c-slot-id="customer_review-R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-csa-c-type="widget" data-hook="review" class="a-section aok-relative" data-csa-c-id="ihnhb0-bts5ba-gohnrc-r0mxzp"><div data-hook="genome-widget" class="a-row a-spacing-mini"><a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AHUDO3JUUGDNW2UQT6CRIERD7EHQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top" data-csa-c-slot-id="customer_review-R2M2W4NUQ69ZI_profile" data-csa-c-type="element" class="a-profile _Y3Itd_profile-link_2n23E" data-a-size="small" data-csa-c-id="81yc4w-yall50-qf9cbf-j1x3sc"><div aria-hidden="true" class="a-profile-avatar-wrapper"><div class="a-profile-avatar"><img src="./fullstar-chopper_files/grey-pixel.gif" class="a-lazy-loaded" data-src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/78970d42-cc2f-4b10-89b1-88761b124b95._CR0%2C0%2C1125%2C1125_SX460_SX48_.jpg"><noscript><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/78970d42-cc2f-4b10-89b1-88761b124b95._CR0%2C0%2C1125%2C1125_SX460_SX48_.jpg"/></noscript></div></div><div class="a-profile-content"><span class="a-profile-name">Emily A</span></div></a></div><div class="_Y3Itd_single-review-star-rating-bar-desktop_1T97A"><i data-hook="review-star-rating" class="a-icon a-icon-star a-star-3"><span class="a-icon-alt">3 out of 5 stars</span></i><span class="a-letter-space"></span></div><a class="a-size-base a-color-base a-link-normal a-text-bold" href="https://www.amazon.com/portal/customer-reviews/srp/-/R2M2W4NUQ69ZI/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_ttl?_encoding=UTF8&amp;ie=UTF8"><h5 class="_Y3Itd_single-review-title_2aKRE" data-hook="reviewTitle" lang="en-US">Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore</h5></a><div data-hook="review-by-line" class="a-row a-spacing-none"><span data-hook="review-date" class="a-size-base a-color-tertiary">Reviewed in the United States on March 29, 2026</span></div><div data-hook="product-variation-attributes" class="a-row a-spacing-mini"><a data-hook="format-strip" class="a-link-normal" href="https://www.amazon.com/portal/customer-reviews/B0B8SQKDCL/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_fmt?_encoding=UTF8&amp;formatType=current_format"><span class="a-size-base a-color-secondary">Color: Black<i class="a-icon a-icon-text-separator" role="presentation"></i></span><span class="a-size-base a-color-secondary">Size: 4 in 1</span></a><i class="a-icon a-icon-text-separator" role="presentation"></i><span class="_Y3Itd_inline-contributor_33jDb"><div data-hook="review-badges"><a class="a-link-normal" href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_avp?ie=UTF8&amp;nodeId=G8UYX7LALQC8V9KA"><span data-hook="avp-badge" class="a-size-mini a-color-state a-text-bold">Verified Purchase</span></a></div></span></div><div data-hook="reviewTextContainer" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-text-container_325WM"><div data-hook="reviewText" class="a-cardui-deck _Y3Itd_card-deck_37S9P" data-a-remove-top-gutter="true" data-a-remove-bottom-gutter="true" name="a-cardui-deck-autoname-9"><div class="a-teaser-describedby-collapsed a-hidden" id="a-cardui-deck-autoname-9-teaser-describedby-collapsed">Brief content visible, double tap to read full content.</div><div class="a-teaser-describedby-expanded a-hidden" id="a-cardui-deck-autoname-9-teaser-describedby-expanded">Full content visible, double tap to read brief content.</div><div data-csa-c-slot-id="true" data-csa-c-type="element" class="a-cardui _Y3Itd_peek-expand_3G9Ub" data-a-card-type="peekExpand" name="a-cardui-deck-autoname-9-card0" data-csa-c-id="ozllkr-edirwr-epfb3c-2mcwbi"><div class="a-cardui-body _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-reactive-container a-reactive-container-transition"><div><div class="a-cardui-content a-cardui-uninitialized" data-a-max-height="300" style="max-height:300px"><div class="_Y3Itd_relative_1SChh"><div data-hook="reviewRichContentContainer" lang="en-US" class="_Y3Itd_contain-rich-content_2IORW"><p><span>I purchased this vegetable chopper in mid-2023 to make meal prep more efficient and slightly more fun, but after over a year, my feelings are mixed. The assembly is straightforward as the different blade options snap and lock into the base easily, and the overall fit of the components is secure. It has a clean, professional appearance on the counter, but the actual functionality depends entirely on what you are trying to chop.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>While the machine offers versatility with several blade options, it doesn't meet the bar for everything in my kitchen. Soft vegetables like tomatoes are not good candidates as they tend to get smashed, and very hard vegetables like carrots are too difficult to push through. For me, it really only works well for bell peppers and onions, and even then, you have to cut the vegetables down significantly first unless you want to throw your entire body weight into it.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>The biggest drawback for me is the cleanup. The blades are not the easiest to clean, and even using the provided plastic claw, removing debris is rarely effortless. Since I only regularly use it for two types of vegetables and then freeze them in batches, I don't feel it provides great value for the money for my specific household. However, I can see where someone who chops a much wider variety of moderate-density produce daily would get more use out of this.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>One final thought on the design: I really wish the collection bowl was made of glass instead of plastic. Given how much pressure you have to apply to chop certain items, glass would feel much more durable and wouldn't be prone to the staining or scratching that plastic eventually develops.</span></p></div></div></div></div><div class="a-reactive-container-gradient"></div></div></div><div data-hook="reviewExpandButtonContainer" class="a-cardui-footer _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer _Y3Itd_read-more-less_2uDYd" data-csa-c-type="widget" data-csa-interaction-events="click" data-csa-c-id="f0j5xr-3rhrhh-7cwyx9-s2ywwu"><a href="javascript:void(0)" class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer-button" role="button"><span class="a-expander-icon"><i class="a-css-icon a-css-icon-draw a-css-icon-expand"></i></span><span class="a-see-more a-color-link"><span class="a-see-more-text" style="">Read more</span><span class="a-see-less-text" style="display:none">Read less</span></span></a></div></div></div></div><div data-hook="translationSpinner" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-translation-spinner-container_ypxf2" style="display: none !important;"><div class="a-spinner-wrapper _Y3Itd_single-review-translation-spinner_1tBUJ"><span class="a-spinner a-spinner-medium"></span></div></div></div><div class="a-section a-spacing-small"><div class="a-section a-spacing-none _Y3Itd_single-review-image-tile-section_15c2C"><button class="_Y3Itd_single-review-thumbnail-container_9KgXc" data-mix-operations="SingleReviewMediaImageThumbnailClickHandler" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-physicalid="71VkNcDJPaL"><img alt="Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71VkNcDJPaL._SY500_.jpg" data-hook="review-image-tile" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-image-tile_3c5HW"></button><button class="_Y3Itd_single-review-thumbnail-container_9KgXc" data-mix-operations="SingleReviewMediaImageThumbnailClickHandler" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-physicalid="71iyDFjZ5dL"><img alt="Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71iyDFjZ5dL._SY500_.jpg" data-hook="review-image-tile" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-image-tile_3c5HW"></button><button class="_Y3Itd_single-review-thumbnail-container_9KgXc" data-mix-operations="SingleReviewMediaImageThumbnailClickHandler" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-physicalid="71apIiAc2tL"><img alt="Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71apIiAc2tL._SY500_.jpg" data-hook="review-image-tile" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-image-tile_3c5HW"></button><div id="mediaModal_R2M2W4NUQ69ZI"><div class="a-popover-preload" id="a-popover-cr-top-reviews-media-modal_R2M2W4NUQ69ZI"><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-header-container_1kb6I"></div><div class="_Y3Itd_single-review-media-popover-container_FDNFG" data-hook="media-popover-container"><div class="_Y3Itd_modal-content-container_1p_Aj" data-csa-c-type="widget" data-reviewbind="SingleReviewMediaBlock" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-csa-c-slot-id="cm_cr_image_popover" data-closebuttonaria="" data-modaltitlearia="" data-hook="modal-content-container" data-csa-c-id="32lxh5-8vm61k-jq1u63-np0zz4"><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-body-container_3kalb"><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-media-container_39x8v"><button class="_Y3Itd_left-icon-container_1saao" data-mix-operations="leftClickHandler"><span class="_Y3Itd_cr-icon_S_3MZ"><img role="img" aria-label="" class="_Y3Itd_button-icon_1Xsqv" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/23pID5Mp1WTA-31.svg"></span></button><div data-reviewbind="MainMedia" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-modal-media-list-view-container_1uARM"><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-image-view-container_1XEVZ" data-mediaid="71VkNcDJPaL" data-lazyimagesource="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71VkNcDJPaL.jpg" data-csa-c-type="element" data-csa-c-slot-id="cm_cr_image_popover_71VkNcDJPaL_0" data-csa-c-id="78m27m-ezvalf-kyojxo-e10gue"><img alt="Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71VkNcDJPaL._SY500_.jpg" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-image-view_1J8fN"></div><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-image-view-container_1XEVZ" data-mediaid="71iyDFjZ5dL" data-lazyimagesource="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71iyDFjZ5dL.jpg" data-csa-c-type="element" data-csa-c-slot-id="cm_cr_image_popover_71iyDFjZ5dL_1" data-csa-c-id="rcffq2-2pbe19-286igj-oipcwz"><img alt="Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71iyDFjZ5dL._SY500_.jpg" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-image-view_1J8fN"></div><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-image-view-container_1XEVZ" data-mediaid="71apIiAc2tL" data-lazyimagesource="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71apIiAc2tL.jpg" data-csa-c-type="element" data-csa-c-slot-id="cm_cr_image_popover_71apIiAc2tL_2" data-csa-c-id="5z17ia-h3a65r-hgtdb-pi8wz1"><img alt="Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71apIiAc2tL._SY500_.jpg" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-image-view_1J8fN"></div></div><button class="_Y3Itd_right-icon-container_2ryP4" data-mix-operations="rightClickHandler"><span class="_Y3Itd_cr-icon_S_3MZ"><img role="img" aria-label="" class="_Y3Itd_button-icon_1Xsqv" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/7D8iRtQ0DrKAF4O.svg"></span></button></div><div class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-review-container_1w2Ex"><div class="a-section _Y3Itd_cr-media-popover-sidepanel-container_2rHXZ"><div class="a-section a-spacing-small _Y3Itd_cr-media-popover-sidepanel-header-section_KhwYb"><div data-hook="genome-widget" class="a-row a-spacing-mini"><a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AHUDO3JUUGDNW2UQT6CRIERD7EHQ" data-csa-c-slot-id="profile" data-csa-c-type="element" class="a-profile _Y3Itd_profile-link_2n23E" data-a-size="small" data-csa-c-id="ifqq4c-tusqcj-wasqxm-2s7fv5"><div aria-hidden="true" class="a-profile-avatar-wrapper"><div class="a-profile-avatar"><img src="./fullstar-chopper_files/grey-pixel.gif" class="a-lazy-loaded" data-src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/78970d42-cc2f-4b10-89b1-88761b124b95._CR0%2C0%2C1125%2C1125_SX460_SX48_.jpg" style=""><noscript><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/78970d42-cc2f-4b10-89b1-88761b124b95._CR0%2C0%2C1125%2C1125_SX460_SX48_.jpg"/></noscript></div></div><div class="a-profile-content"><span class="a-profile-name">Emily A</span></div></a></div><div class="a-section a-spacing-none"><div class="_Y3Itd_single-review-star-rating-bar-desktop_1T97A"><i data-hook="review-star-rating" class="a-icon a-icon-star a-star-3"><span class="a-icon-alt">3 out of 5 stars</span></i><span class="a-letter-space"></span></div><a class="a-size-base a-color-base a-link-normal a-text-bold" href="https://www.amazon.com/portal/customer-reviews/srp/-/R2M2W4NUQ69ZI/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_ttl?_encoding=UTF8&amp;ie=UTF8"><h5 class="_Y3Itd_single-review-title_2aKRE" data-hook="reviewTitle" lang="en-US">Great for Certain Veggies but the Cleanup is a Chore</h5></a><div data-hook="review-by-line" class="a-row a-spacing-none"><span data-hook="review-date" class="a-size-base a-color-tertiary">Reviewed in the United States on March 29, 2026</span></div><div data-hook="product-variation-attributes" class="a-row a-spacing-mini"><a data-hook="format-strip" class="a-link-normal" href="https://www.amazon.com/portal/customer-reviews/B0B8SQKDCL/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_fmt?_encoding=UTF8&amp;formatType=current_format"><span class="a-size-base a-color-secondary">Color: Black<i class="a-icon a-icon-text-separator" role="presentation"></i></span><span class="a-size-base a-color-secondary">Size: 4 in 1</span></a><i class="a-icon a-icon-text-separator" role="presentation"></i><span class="_Y3Itd_inline-contributor_33jDb"><div data-hook="review-badges"><a class="a-link-normal" href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_avp?ie=UTF8&amp;nodeId=G8UYX7LALQC8V9KA"><span data-hook="avp-badge" class="a-size-mini a-color-state a-text-bold">Verified Purchase</span></a></div></span></div></div><p><span>I purchased this vegetable chopper in mid-2023 to make meal prep more efficient and slightly more fun, but after over a year, my feelings are mixed. The assembly is straightforward as the different blade options snap and lock into the base easily, and the overall fit of the components is secure. It has a clean, professional appearance on the counter, but the actual functionality depends entirely on what you are trying to chop.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>While the machine offers versatility with several blade options, it doesn't meet the bar for everything in my kitchen. Soft vegetables like tomatoes are not good candidates as they tend to get smashed, and very hard vegetables like carrots are too difficult to push through. For me, it really only works well for bell peppers and onions, and even then, you have to cut the vegetables down significantly first unless you want to throw your entire body weight into it.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>The biggest drawback for me is the cleanup. The blades are not the easiest to clean, and even using the provided plastic claw, removing debris is rarely effortless. Since I only regularly use it for two types of vegetables and then freeze them in batches, I don't feel it provides great value for the money for my specific household. However, I can see where someone who chops a much wider variety of moderate-density produce daily would get more use out of this.</span></p><p><span></span></p><p><span>One final thought on the design: I really wish the collection bowl was made of glass instead of plastic. Given how much pressure you have to apply to chop certain items, glass would feel much more durable and wouldn't be prone to the staining or scratching that plastic eventually develops.</span></p><ul class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-thumbnail-image-container_2nWBS" data-reviewbind="MediaThumbnailsBlock"><li class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-list-item-style_d1lj6" data-reviewbind="MediaThumbnail"><button data-mediaid="71VkNcDJPaL" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-thumbidx="0" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-thumbnail-image-button_2LRc_" data-mix-operations="thumbnailClickHandler" aria-pressed="false"><img alt="" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71VkNcDJPaL.jpg" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-thumbnail-image-view_2J_oP" height="80" width="80"></button></li><li class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-list-item-style_d1lj6" data-reviewbind="MediaThumbnail"><button data-mediaid="71iyDFjZ5dL" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-thumbidx="1" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-thumbnail-image-button_2LRc_" data-mix-operations="thumbnailClickHandler" aria-pressed="false"><img alt="" src="./fullstar-chopper_files/71iyDFjZ5dL.jpg" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-thumbnail-image-view_2J_oP" height="80" width="80"></button></li><li class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-list-item-style_d1lj6" data-reviewbind="MediaThumbnail"><button data-mediaid="71apIiAc2tL" data-reviewid="R2M2W4NUQ69ZI" data-thumbidx="2" class="_Y3Itd_media-popover-thumbnail-image-button_2LRc_" data-mix-operations="thumbnailClickHandler" aria-pressed="false"><img alt="" src="./fullstar-choppe